        "note": "Younger Yonaguni speakers are L1 Japanese speakers, and L2 Yonaguni learners (most people under 40 who learn are involved in traditional Okinawan culture, like the theater, with a growing number of language activists). And basically no children learn it at home from their parents, though there have been efforts to establish a language nest. [Endangerment.Certainty: 1]",
